# pre-push leak guard — forbidden-substring blocklist (TEMPLATE)
# ==============================================================
# Copy this file to .githooks/blocklist (which is gitignored) and add one
# forbidden term per line. The pre-push hook treats every non-empty,
# non-comment line as a CASE-INSENSITIVE substring; if any term appears in an
# added diff line or a commit message, the push is blocked.
#
#   cp .githooks/blocklist.example .githooks/blocklist
#   # then edit .githooks/blocklist with your real terms
#
# Why external + gitignored: this repo is PUBLIC. Hardcoding real brand or
# personal names in a versioned file would itself leak them. Keep the real
# list local-only.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# Put the consumer brand names, internal project codenames, personal names,
# emails, and anything else app-specific that must never reach the public
# history here. Generic examples only below — replace them:

acme
johndoe
mycompany
